# rantai-kb (Rust) dev stack — copy to .env and edit.
#
#   cp rust/deploy/.env.example rust/deploy/.env
#
# Docker Compose reads this file automatically because it sits next to
# compose.yaml; anything exported in your shell wins over it. Every setting here
# is optional: without a .env the stack runs with the defaults shown (the
# commented value is the default). Nothing in this file is a real secret; the
# credentials are the local dev ones from rust/scripts/stack-up.sh.
#
# Two rules worth knowing:
#   * A variable that is PRESENT wins over the KB_TIER preset, even when empty.
#     `KB_CACHE_DIR=` therefore means "no disk cache", not "use the default".
#   * Changing tiers with existing data is not supported: lite/lite-en embed at
#     384 dimensions, everything else at 1024. Run `rust/scripts/kb-dev.sh down -v`
#     before switching between those two classes.

# ─── Host ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Host port for kb-server. Change it if 8080 is taken; stores publish nothing.
KB_PORT=8080

# Ports/hostnames are otherwise fixed by the compose network; kb-server always
# listens on 8080 inside its container.

# ─── Build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cargo parallelism for the image build. 2 keeps a shared dev machine usable;
# unset uses all cores.
# CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2

# Tag for the built image (all six tiers share one image).
# KB_IMAGE_TAG=dev

# Reported by GET /health so you can tell which build is running.
# KB_VERSION=dev

# ─── Dev store credentials (local only, not secrets) ────────────────────────

# POSTGRES_USER=kb
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=kb
# POSTGRES_DB=rantai_kb

# SURREAL_DB_USER=root
# SURREAL_DB_PASS=root
# SURREAL_DB_NAMESPACE=rantai
# SURREAL_DB_DATABASE=knowledge

# rustfs (S3) credentials; it reads these as MINIO_ROOT_USER/PASSWORD.
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=kbadmin
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=kbsecret123
# S3_BUCKET=rantai-kb
# S3_REGION=us-east-1

# ─── Models and inference ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local tiers only (lite, lite-en, desk, studio, station): the tier preset points
# these at loopback, which is wrong inside compose, so compose.yaml substitutes
# the service hostname. Setting them here wins over that substitution — use it to
# run the models on another machine instead of in this stack.
#
# An OpenAI-compatible embedding server (llama.cpp `llama-server --embedding`,
# vLLM, another TEI) and a reranker:
#
#   KB_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8081/v1/embeddings
#   KB_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=local
#   KB_RERANK_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8082/v1/rerank
#   KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=cohere
#
# KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=cohere is what llama.cpp's /v1/rerank takes (the Cohere
# request shape) and KB_RERANK_BASE_URL is then the full endpoint. For another
# TEI, keep KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=tei and give the base URL without /rerank.
# KB_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://tei-lite:80/v1/embeddings
# KB_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=local-tei
# KB_RERANK_PROVIDER=tei
# KB_RERANK_BASE_URL=http://tei-rerank-desk:80

# CPU budget for the lite/lite-en embedder and kb-server. Ingest on a 2-core box
# ran with one thread for the embedder and a core left for the server; raise both
# together on a bigger machine (and KB_EMBED_THREADS with them).
# KB_LITE_EMBED_CPUS=1.0
# KB_LITE_SERVER_CPUS=1.0
# KB_EMBED_THREADS=1

# TEI image for the GPU tiers. The plain tag is CUDA; use :<ver>-turing for
# Turing-class cards, or a rocm- tag for AMD.
# TEI_GPU_IMAGE=ghcr.io/huggingface/text-embeddings-inference:1.8.1

# ─── Spend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cloud only (paid). `kb-dev.sh up cloud` refuses to start without it.
# Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys — do not commit the value.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ─── Ingest / retrieval extras (all off by default, all free) ───────────────

# Local tiers keep entity extraction off and use the heuristic extractor, so a
# stray OpenRouter key is never spent by an ingest. Set both to turn the graph on:
#   KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=true
#   KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTOR=heuristic   # or llm to pay OpenRouter
#   KB_GRAPH_STORE=pg
#   KB_GRAPH_ARM=true
# KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=false
# KB_ENTITY_EXTRACTOR=heuristic
# KB_GRAPH_STORE=none
# KB_GRAPH_ARM=false

# Content-addressed embedding/extraction cache inside the container. It lives on
# the kb-cache volume and survives `down` (not `down -v`). Set it empty to disable
# caching — every ingest then pays for its embeddings again.
# KB_CACHE_DIR=/app/cache

# Log level for the server (`RUST_LOG` syntax).
# RUST_LOG=info
